- The **30 anti-template warning signals** above come from the user-supplied image headed “30 reasons your site looks vibecoded.” They are interpreted as heuristics, not objectively validated rules.
- The starting principles (avoid generic gradient/glass aesthetics, enforce spacing and design tokens, prefer structured hierarchy, and use semantic frontend code) are adapted and expanded from the user's original `Design.mdc`.
- The named design trends are adapted from Figma's web-design-trends guide, accessed for this rule in **October 2026**. Always refresh trend research when tools are available; do not assume this document stays current indefinitely.
- The inspiration URLs are research starting points only. Some galleries may block automated browsing or show illustrative work that differs from production behavior.
- Accessibility, truthful content, and user task completion outrank stylistic trends or awards-gallery novelty.
